\end{array}$$ Here $c_0^{\pm}$ and $\widetilde{c}_0^{\pm}$ are given in  and   and $\chi_0:{\mathbb{R}}\setminus\{V'(0),V'(1)\}\to{\mathbb{R}}$ is defined by $$\label{eq:chi0largetime}
\chi_0(k,t) \equiv 
H(u^*(k))+
\log \left(\frac{4 k^2-v_0^{\infty}(k,t)^2}{4 (u^*(k)-1) u^*(k) v_0^{\infty}(k,t)^{3/2} \sqrt{V''(u^*(k))}}\right),$$ with $V$ and $H$ given in  and $u^*$ in . We now state the main result of the section, namely an expansion for the forward smile in all regimes and (log) strikes on the real line. The proof is given in Section \[sec:fwdsmileproofnonsteeplargemat\].

\[theorem:HestonLargeMatFwdSmileNonSteep\] The following expansion holds for the forward smile as $\tau$ tends to infinity: $$\sigma_{t,\tau}^2(k\tau)
=
v_0^{\infty}(k,t)+v_1^{\infty}(k,t)\tau^{-\lambda}+{\mathcal{R}}(\tau,\lambda),
\qquad\text{for any }k\in{\mathbb{R}},$$ where $v_1^{\infty}:{\mathbb{R}}\times{\mathbb{R}}_{+}\to{\mathbb{R}}$ is defined by $$v_1^{\infty}(k,t)
